  data: {
    LLM: "Keep track of the Aces. In a 32-card deck, Aces are nearly impossible to beat unless someone trumps. If you have the lead, play your Aces early to secure point-tricks before the opponent can void a suit.\n\nTrump Management: Use the exchange (if allowed in your variant) to build a 'Long Suit'. If you can control the trump suit with 4-5 cards, you can dominate the end-game and capture the opponent's high-value side cards.\n\nThe 'Seven Swap': If you have the 7 of trumps, don't swap it too early. Wait until the opponent leads a high trump, then swap and play the new trump to seize the lead. This defensive move can break their momentum.",
    Player: "Keep track of the Aces. In a 32-card deck, Aces are nearly impossible to beat unless someone trumps. If you have the lead, play your Aces early to secure point-tricks before the opponent can void a suit.\n\nTrump Management: Use the exchange (if allowed in your variant) to build a 'Long Suit'. If you can control the trump suit with 4-5 cards, you can dominate the end-game and capture the opponent's high-value side cards.\n\nThe 'Seven Swap': If you have the 7 of trumps, don't swap it too early. Wait until the opponent leads a high trump, then swap and play the new trump to seize the lead. This defensive move can break their momentum.",
